{#
   Period Awards (#period-awards) — who WON last period on each awarding leaderboard.

   This is NOT a revival of the orphaned _leaderboards.html.twig. That file is a
   12-tab, JS-fetched widget over /api/leaderboard/{category}: current standings,
   client-fetched, live. This is the opposite — who won a period that has ENDED,
   frozen at close, server-rendered, with no API endpoint behind it. Restoring the
   orphan stays a one-line include and the two do not conflict; see
   index.html.twig's own header comment.

   Placed between _owner_spotlight and _testers deliberately: the Rich List
   already establishes the leaderboard reading mode there, and two ranked boards
   back to back is the design's own grouping.

   A period board scores GROWTH during the period, not the all-time total — which
   is why a club nobody has heard of can top one, and why the sub-label says
   "gained" rather than "total". The score is already the growth value; nothing
   here recomputes it.

   Every value is frozen on the archive row: club name, kit, badge, country, the
   named performer, and the period's own start/end instants. Nothing is read off
   the live Club, which is what lets a club that has since been DELETED still
   render its badge — the page's "any club listed anywhere shows at least its
   badge" rule.

   Own .lbaw-* namespace, borrowing the gold-ringed panel family from
   .ospot-*/.spotlight-* without sharing their classes — the same precedent that
   keeps those two from silently restyling each other.

   Sprites are composed CLIENT-SIDE from data-club-badge, by landing.js's
   mountPeriodAwards() through the shared clubBadgeIconsHtml(). The JS hooks are
   load-bearing: it walks `.lbaw-row`, then `.lbaw-club-badge` within it.

   Renders nothing when periodAwards is empty, which is the real state until an
   admin enables an award definition and a period ends. _nav.html.twig gates its
   jump link on the same emptiness check, exactly as .nav-spotlight-cta is gated
   on spotlight.isLive.
#}
{% if periodAwards is not empty %}
<section class="lbaw-section" id="period-awards" aria-labelledby="lbaw-title">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-label">Period Awards</div>
        <div class="lbaw-board-head">
            <h2 class="pixel" id="lbaw-title">LAST PERIOD'S WINNERS</h2>
            <span class="lbaw-header-sub vt">Closed and settled — the prize is already in the winner's inbox</span>
        </div>

        <div class="lbaw-grid">
            {% for board in periodAwards %}
                <article class="lbaw-board">
                    <header class="lbaw-board-title">
                        <h3 class="lbaw-name pixel">{{ board.name }}</h3>
                        <span class="lbaw-period vt">
                            {# The frozen instants, never re-derived from the period key. #}
                            {{ board.cadenceLabel|upper }} &middot; {{ board.periodLabel }}
                        </span>
                    </header>

                    {# <ol>: the ranking is the content, so it lives in the markup and not
                       only in the rendered rank glyph. #}
                    <ol class="lbaw-rows">
                        {% for entry in board.entries %}
                            <li class="lbaw-row{{ entry.awarded ? ' lbaw-row-awarded' : '' }}"
                                data-club-badge="{{ {home: entry.homeKitConfig, away: entry.awayKitConfig, badge: entry.badgeConfig}|json_encode|e('html_attr') }}">

                                <span class="lbaw-rank pixel">
                                    <span class="visually-hidden">Rank </span>{{ '%02d'|format(entry.rank) }}
                                </span>

                                <span class="lbaw-club-badge" aria-hidden="true"></span>

                                <span class="lbaw-club">
                                    <span class="lbaw-club-name">{{ entry.clubName }}</span>
                                    {% if entry.displayLabel %}
                                        {# The performer who scored IN THAT PERIOD, frozen —
                                           the live row overwrites it next week, which is the
                                           whole point of freezing it. #}
                                        <span class="lbaw-performer vt">{{ entry.displayLabel }}</span>
                                    {% endif %}
                                </span>

                                <span class="lbaw-score">
                                    <span class="lbaw-score-val pixel">{{ entry.score|number_format }}</span>
                                    <span class="lbaw-score-lbl vt">GAINED</span>
                                </span>

                                {% if entry.awarded %}
                                    <span class="lbaw-prize pixel" title="Prize delivered to this club's inbox">
                                        <span class="visually-hidden">Prize place </span>&#9733;
                                    </span>
                                {% endif %}
                            </li>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </ol>

                    <footer class="lbaw-board-foot vt">
                        {{ board.entryCount|number_format }} {{ board.entryCount == 1 ? 'club' : 'clubs' }} competed
                        {% if board.awardCount > 0 %}
                            &middot; {{ board.awardCount }} {{ board.awardCount == 1 ? 'prize' : 'prizes' }} paid
                        {% endif %}
                    </footer>
                </article>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>

        <p class="lbaw-note">
            Each board is a closed period, scored on what a club <strong>gained</strong> during it
            rather than on its all-time total — so a period is winnable by a club that is not the
            all-time leader. Archived at close and never recalculated.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>
{% endif %}
